     "set": {
      "tone": "accent"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "note",
     "set": {
      "text": "scope of ∀x: the bracket after it",
      "tone": "accent"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Inside that bracket, ∃y owns the y in R(x, y). Its scope is just R(x, y).",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "t4",
     "set": {
      "tone": "info",
      "fill": "info"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "t5",
     "set": {
      "tone": "info",
      "fill": "info"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "note",
     "set": {
      "text": "scope of ∃y: R(x, y)",
      "tone": "info"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "The x in P(x) and in R(x, y) are inside the scope of ∀x: they are bound.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "t2",
     "set": {
      "tone": "success",
      "fill": "success"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "t5",
     "set": {
      "tone": "success",
      "fill": "success"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "note2",
     "set": {
      "text": "bound: x in P(x), x and y in R(x, y)",
      "tone": "success"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "The bracket closes before ∧. The x in Q(x) is outside every quantifier on x: it is free.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "t8",
     "set": {
      "tone": "danger",
      "fill": "danger"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "note",
     "set": {
      "text": "the x in Q(x) is free",
      "tone": "danger"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "A formula with a free variable is not a sentence: its value depends on what x is. To cover Q(x) too, bracket the whole conjunction after ∀x.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "note2",
     "set": {
      "text": "fix: ∀x ((P(x) → ∃y R(x, y)) ∧ Q(x))",
      "tone": "accent"
     }
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
